{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>To his father and to his mother he did not see him.</b> If his father or mother, brother or son dies, he must treat him as one he does not recognize, as it is written: לאביו ולאמו לא יטמא. And why <b>for they kept your word</b> — that you said: ומן המקדש לא יצא, even in his time of distress he is not permitted to go out after them. And even according to the one who says מקדושתו לא יצא, but he does go out after the deceased — in any case, when they are uncovered he is covered, and when they are covered he is uncovered. Another interpretation: <b>he said to his father and to his mother, I did not see him</b> — they did not go astray after them in the matter of the calf." "<b>And your covenant they shall keep.</b> What you said: the covenant of an everlasting priesthood."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "Resolved the abbreviations מ״ד as 'the one who says' and מ״מ as 'in any case' (literally 'from that which'). The subject of the last sentence is ambiguous in the Hebrew; rendered literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:23.599416070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}